# Ch9 Poisoning

## Comprehensive evaluation of the poisoned patient

- **Salient points of Hx:**
  - **HPI** - details from witnesses of the circumstances of the OD:
    - What toxins have been taken?
    - How much of the toxin have been taken?
    - What time was the toxin taken?
    - What route is the toxin taken through?
    - Has alcohol or any other drugs misused as well?
  - **PMH** - GP for background PMH and detailed drug Hx
  - **Other relevant Hx:**
    - SHx, FHx, allergic Hx
    - Psychiatric evaluation and suicide risk
    - Mental capacity for accepting or refusing Tx
- **P/E:** ![](img/approach_to_evaluation_of_poisoned_patient.png) 
![](img/clinical_signs_of_drugs_of_misuse.png)

